	abstract = {In the age of artificial intelligence (AI), the healthcare industry should transform itself to provide better care and services. AI plays a critical role in healthcare; future healthcare professionals have to be trained about the use of AI so that the systems work seamlessly and they will harness the capabilities of AI to improve patient care and bring more innovation into this industry. It must inculcate unique blend skills such as AI literacy, clinical expertise, critical thinking, collaboration, emotional intelligence, data analysis, innovation, ethics, and responsibility. It will be incumbent upon educational institutions and healthcare organizations to incorporate AI-centred curricula and training programmes into their instructional agendas and provide hands-on experience with AI tools and technologies. It is important to foster interdisciplinary collaboration between healthcare professionals, data scientists, and AI experts to encourage continuous learning and professional development, and finally, develop AI-related competencies and assessment frameworks. By educating and training the next generation of healthcare professionals in AI, we can improve patient care and outcomes with AI-driven insights, enhance operational efficiency and lower costs, drive innovation and entrepreneurship in healthcare, address healthcare workforce shortages and develop new career paths, assure responsible AI adoption, and address ethical concerns. As such, this chapter will review the types of competencies needed to train the new generation of healthcare professionals in AI to change it in accordance with a fast-changing healthcare landscape and to improve the care of patients and ensure economic growth. Therefore, it will show how much education systems now centre towards AI-based education and training in the health workforce. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Babita Singla, Kumar Shalender, Nripendra Singh, and Sandhir Sharma; individual chapters, the contrib