	abstract = {Ensuring sustainable water quality management in the face of climate change, urbanization, and industrialization demands systems that are both intelligent and transparent. This study introduces a novel Explainable AI (XAI) driven framework specifically designed for real-time water quality monitoring and management. The proposed system integrates IoT-based data collection, hybrid cloud-edge preprocessing, interpretable machine learning, and ethical oversight to ensure transparency, trust, and actionable insights. Unlike conventional black-box models, our architecture embeds XAI modules across the entire pipeline from inference to optimization to provide stakeholders with interpretable predictions, anomaly alerts, and resource recommendations. A key innovation lies in the incorporation of fairness aware decision support and ethical transparency checks, ensuring equitable outcomes in diverse water ecosystems. This paper not only surveys existing efforts from 2018-2025 but also positions the proposed system as a robust, scalable solution that overcomes limitations in model generalizability and interpretability. Future directions include fusing participatory sensing with edge-based XAI inference to accelerate citizendriven, sustainable water governance. © 2025 IEEE.},
