	affiliations = {CA, United States},
	abstract = {Generative AI is reshaping the product management function across strategy, execution, and cross-functional collaboration. As tools like ChatGPT, NotebookLM, Gemini, and Zoom AI Companion become embedded in daily workflows, product managers (PMs) are not just delegating tasks but are assuming a new role as orchestrators of hybrid human-AI workflows. This paper synthesizes qualitative observations from real-world GenAI use cases, industry reports, and empirical studies to examine how GenAI is augmenting product managers across four dimensions: scope of responsibilities, team collaboration, skill requirements, and strategic decision-making. Drawing on practitioner experience and emerging frameworks like Anthropic's 4D AI Fluency model, this paper offers practical insights into how PMs are using GenAI to generate PRDs, analyze market gaps, manage AI risks, and accelerate cross-functional alignment. Rather than replacing PMs, GenAI amplifies their ability to act as strategic leaders, though not without challenges. It examines technical integration barriers, bias and governance concerns, and access inequities, while providing actionable best practices. This paper aims to equip product leaders, engineering managers, and PMs with a practical, end-to-end framework for responsibly leveraging GenAI in modern product organizations.  © 2025 IEEE.},
