	affiliations = {University of the Cumberlands, Department of Information Technology, Williamsburg, 40769, KY, United States; Dr. D. Y. Patil School of Science and Technology, Dr. D. Y. Patil Vidyapeeth, Tathawade, Pune, 411033, India; Sai Info Solution, Maharashtra, Nashik, India; Sri Eshwar College of Engineering, Department of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Tamil Nadu, Coimbatore, India},
	abstract = {As the concern about data privacy risks in AI applications (especially in sensitive areas like healthcare) is mounting, traditional and centralized learning models create serious risks. This study will help to develop a privacypreserving and trustworthy AI framework by developing a combined approach on Federated Learning (FL) with blockchain technology. This framework enables model training at the edge with decentralized model training, meaning that data is kept locally and only model updates are stored on the blockchain; each model update is stored on the blockchain and the updates are validated and secured through smart contracts on the blockchain registered for the learning framework by each partner. There is the addition of off-chain storage and the implementation of differential privacy for performance and security measures in optimizing the model learning. Evaluation by experimentation with CIFAR-10, MNIST, Healthcare, and Fashion MNIST data shows accuracy improvements of nearly 2.4% and communication costs reduced against FL standard methods. The evaluations demonstrate the robustness, efficiency, and privacy protection of the framework. Therefore, this research provides a pathway to the development of secure and scalable AI systems, and is particularly pertinent for use in ethical, socially responsible and regulation-compliant deployments. © 2025 IEEE.},
