	abstract = {PhotoSensei introduces a theoretical framework for an AI-powered, mobile photography tutor that delivers real-time, personalized feedback by integrating lightweight computer-vision encoders with large-language-model–driven guidance. We bridge a critical gap in mobile learning static tutorials and post-hoc critiques by proposing a hybrid CV-LLM loop that (1) analyzes compositional and technical image features in situ, (2) generates adaptive natural-language feedback aligned with learner proficiency, and (3) embeds reflection–practice cycles to foster deeper skill acquisition. Our conceptual model formalizes core constructs “Photography Feedback” dimensions and “Skill-Level Personalization” and articulates three testable propositions on reflection, engagement, and learning transfer. We further delineate a four-phase research roadmap, guiding future PoC expansions toward empirical validation, reinforcement-learning–driven adaptation, and scalable deployment. By situating PhotoSensei at the intersection of intelligent tutoring systems and mobile pedagogy, this work advances theory in AI-mediated creative education and lays the groundwork for next-generation ITS designs in photography and beyond. © 2025 IEEE.},
