	abstract = {As AI is now deep within making decisions in so many sectors, models often don't understand the human emotions and this creates ethical dilemmas and lack of transparency. In order to bridge this gap, this paper proposes Emotionally Intelligent Explainable AI (EIXAI), an integrated Emotional Intelligence (EI) variant of Explainable AI (XAI) systems. The three main components of the EIXAI framework are (1) an Emotional Perception Module; (2) an Ethical Decision-Making Engine (EIDE); and (3) an Explainability & Human-AI Interactions Layer. These components enable the AI systems to infer emotional cues, dynamically reason with ethicality and offer explainable and context aware explanations. As compared to previous systems, EIXAI uses multimodal emotional assessments, reinforcement learning for human adaptive improvement, and real time ethical adaptation to facilitate decisions. Through these two aspects, the proposed approach guarantees fairness, accountability and transparency, while AI decisions align with human's values. These areas of application include healthcare, finance, human resources and autonomous systems relevant to ethical and emotional determination. Research in future will be extended to both better multimodal emotional recognition, and regulatory frameworks as well as decentralized AI governance. Introducing emotional intelligence into AI (EIXAI) enables human cantered AI decision making, which leads to an ethical responsibility towards AI and increased trust on the AI systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
