	abstract = {This study proposes a new artificial intelligence framework- Adaptive Neuro-Empathic Therapeutic Intelligence (ANETI) to help in personalized mental health counseling. ANETI employs emotional resonance mapping, biometric-behavioral data fusion and adaptive learning to provide human-like therapeutic contact interactions. There are four successive steps in the methodology namely multi-modal data integration, the generation of adaptive therapeutic response, real-time learning, and crisis prediction. ANETI proved to be a more efficient tool than conventional therapy and AI chatbots, showing 89 percent of symptom reduction, 94 percent adherence to the treatment, and 96 percent accurate detection of crises during a 12-month clinical trial, including 500 participants. The framework presents 46.7 percent saving per session and 91 percent patient retention thanks to its low-cost and long term effect. Its most significant novelty aspects are empathic neural networks, the contextual memory, and the ethical AI governance. This paper makes ANETI, a pioneer in scalable, emotionally intelligent digital mental health systems with demonstrated efficacy in a variety of demographics.  © 2025 IEEE.},
