	abstract = {This paper introduces a novel approach to semantic parsing that transforms natural language queries into SQL statements using generative AI. Our system, GenSQL, uses a context-aware semantic parsing framework that responds to different database schemes while eliminating tag needings forming domain specific training. In contrast to previous approaches focusing on phrase based schema linking or heavily dependent on complex predefined encoders/genetive models, GenSQL illustrates how large generative models can capture user intent and outperform the syntactically correct SQL on schema aware translation. The system supports multiple input types including text face and speech recognition, and multiple inputs can support dynamic schema adaptation. GenSQL achieves a precision of 9 4 % incomplex analytical queries, surpassing recent methods by 7. 8 %. Analysis of error cases reveals that GenSQL shines particularly in simplifying ambiguous natural language queries and queries that involve complex joins. With support for an array of data formats and the ability to handle unfamiliar schemas, this system is especially useful for non-technical users wanting to analyze different data sets without any SQL training. © 2025 IEEE.},
