	abstract = {Digital marketing ecosystems create high-velocity, high-variety and high-volume traces of interaction across web, mobile, social and point-of-sale channels. These traces must be transformed into trustworthy predictions of customer behavior, and such transformation requires sound feature engineering, scalable learning, sound evaluation, and responsible governance. This article will recommend an AI-based, end-to-end predictive analytics customer behavior modeling (propensity, churn, conversion, next-best-action, and lifetime value) framework. We state the problem as a multi-objective learning and decisiontask, describe a pipeline (ingestion, identity resolution, feature store, model zoo, uplift modeling, and real-time serving) in modules and report the results of a representative benchmark with gradient-boosted trees and sequence models. We follow the latest directions of AI-based marketing and CRM automation. [1]-[11] and address ethical and governance concerns around bias, privacy, and manipulation [12]. The framework achieves state-of-the-art AUC and uplift on multiple behaviors while reducing time-to-decision via real-time inference, and it embeds guardrails (fairness diagnostics, explainability, human-in-theloop) to promote responsible deployment. © 2025 IEEE.},
