	journal = {IETACS 2025 - 2025 International Conference on Innovations and Emerging Technologies in AI and Communication Systems: Unifying AI and Communication for a Smarter Tomorrow},
	pages = {962 - 968},
	doi = {10.1109/IETACS68750.2025.11385374},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105039280969?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {G. Pullaiah College of Engineering and Technology (Autonomous), Department of Management Studies, Andhra Pradesh, Kurnool, India; Karnavati University, Gujarat, Gandhinagar, India; School of Computer Science, Malla Reddy Engineering College for Women (UGC Autonomous), Telangana, Hyderabad, India; Sri Siddhartha Academy of Higher Education, Department of Computer Science, Karnataka, Tumkur, India; Vaish College of Engineering, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Haryana, Rohtak, India; Ambalika Institute of Management & Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Uttar Pradesh, Lucknow, India},
	abstract = {The rapid growth of networked devices, 6G networks, and cloud-edge technologies has made modern communication systems far more complicated and open to assault. Static and reactive security solutions can't keep up with threats in dynamic network settings since they change all the time. Through this study, a framework that is referred to as UAASC is presented with the purpose of improving security, facilitating scalability, and providing real-time accessibility. Federation-based learning, decision-making based on agents, and machine learning are all used in this process. In order to safeguard data while it is being sent across various platforms, the system employs a number of different means, including encryption techniques, anomaly detection techniques, and adaptive response techniques. The results of the simulation demonstrate that this technique is superior to others in terms of locating intrusions, decreasing latency, and minimizing the number of false positives and false negatives. In order to guarantee the security of the communication networks of the future generation, the UAASC design is proactive, pays attention to the situation, and safeguards users' privacy. © 2025 IEEE.},
