	abstract = {The integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Recruitment and Selection (R & S) has revolutionized hiring processes, particularly in Information Technology (IT) and Banking sectors by enhancing efficiency, reducing costs and minimizing human bias. AI driven tools such as Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), Machine Learning (ML) algorithms, Chatbots and predictive analytics streamline candidate screening, optimize talent acquisition and enable data driven hiring decisions. The IT sector has rapidly adopted AI to manage large applicant pools and assess technical competencies while the Banking sector leverages AI for mass recruitment, fraud detection and behavioral assessments. Despite its advantages, challenges like algorithmic bias, lack of transparency and data privacy concerns remain significant. This paper is an attempt to organise the existing studies, structure the relevant outcomes and understand the evolution, benefits and challenges of AI driven hiring, highlighting emerging trends such as explainable AI (XAI), ethical AI governance and AI powered digital interviews and finally suggest a human AI collaboration model to ensure fairness, diversity and effectiveness in hiring decisions.  © 2025 IEEE.},
