	abstract = {This paper examines the transformative impact of autonomous Artificial Intelligence (AI) agents on contemporary brand management. Moving beyond traditional automation, these agents introduce a paradigm shift from retrospective analysis to prospective, simulation-based strategy. We first analyze the evolution of sentiment analysis, detailing how psychographically-grounded AI agents enable predictive modeling of consumer sentiment with high fidelity, allowing brands to pre-emptively manage perception. Second, we explore how these real-time insights facilitate dynamic brand messaging and agile strategy adaptation. Third, the paper investigates the application of AI agents in driving hyper-personalized consumer engagement and conversion, analyzing their quantifiable impact on marketing ROI and customer loyalty. Fourth, we provide a concise overview of the modular architecture that underpins these intelligent systems. Finally, we conduct a critical analysis of the profound ethical challenges, including algorithmic bias, data privacy, and the need for new governance frameworks. We conclude that while AI agents offer unprecedented capabilities for brand optimization, their effective and responsible deployment requires a renewed focus on human-centric strategy, ethical oversight, and brand authenticity.  © 2025 IEEE.},
