	abstract = {The rapid adoption of Artificial Intelligence systems in high-stakes domains such as agriculture underscores the need for trustworthiness. In this paper, we present a chatbot system designed to provide actionable insights for crop commodity markets by leveraging a Retrieval-Augmented Generation framework. The system integrates a Trust Engine to evaluate its performance across key dimensions, including data reliability, source reputation, and user feedback, ensuring accurate and reliable information delivery. The Trust Engine calculates trust scores at two levels: (1) for individual interactions using fuzzy logic and (2) for the system's behavior over time by aggregating metrics such as user feedback, discrepancy counts, and unknown answer rates. We conducted an initial evaluation on ten representative queries commonly encountered by market stakeholders, highlighting variations in response quality and trust scores.The results demonstrate the effectiveness of the Trust Engine in distinguishing between high- and low-trust responses and emphasize the critical role of trust assessment in AI-driven decision support tools. This work lays the foundation for more robust and explainable AI systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
