	abstract = {AI is transforming the concepts of software engineering. Re-engineering legacy methods of Agile, DevOps, and CI/CD are predictive analytics, generative programming, and self-healing automation. Despite these approaches having made the delivery simpler and more responsive, it remains to a great extent rule-based and reactive. The modern AI based systems on the other hand have learning feedbacks which modify the design, testing and deployment behavior. The researcher discusses the effects of intelligent automation on each of the software lifecycle phases and introduces a new Intelligent Software Engineering (ISE) model in this paper with the objective of enhancing the productivity, reliability, and explainability. The case studies and, by the power of quantitative analysis, the framework depict a 35 percent reduction in the build cycle time, 40 percent reduction in the rate of deployment error, and 50 percent reduction in the meantime to resolution (MTTR). Along with the above-mentioned, the paper highlights the need to have human-centred governance to prevent the absence of transparency, bias, and moral drifts in the automated pipelines. Practical recommendations on how to establish transparent, sustainable and responsible AI-aided engineering systems are the final additions to the paper. © 2025 IEEE.},
