	title = {CARESUM: A Verification-Driven Framework for Clinical Dialogue Summarization with an Intelligent Chatbot Interface},
	year = {2025},
	journal = {Proceedings of 2025 International Conference on Signal Processing, Computation, Electronics, Power and Telecommunication, IConSCEPT 2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/IConSCEPT66142.2025.11436852},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105036557113?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Vellore Institute of Technology, School of Computer Science and Engineering, Tamil Nadu, Vellore, India},
	abstract = {Clinical dialogue summarization is the automated process of converting multi-turn doctor-patient conversations into concise, structured summaries that preserve essential medical details. Its primary objective is to reduce the documentation burden on clinicians while maintaining the accuracy of critical information. However, despite recent advances in large language models (LLMs), existing systems often suffer from hallucination-producing fluent but factually incorrect statements. In healthcare, such inaccuracies can negatively impact patient outcomes and clinical decisions. To address these limitations, this study presents CARESUM (Clinical AI for Reliable and Enhanced Summarization), a multi-stage Generator-Verifier-Judge framework designed to enhance factual consistency and interpretability in clinical summaries. The framework first transcribes the conversation using an Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) module. It then uses a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) layer to pull in relevant context, and finally creates an initial summary through the Generator model. A Verifier then classifies each statement as supported, contradicted, or uncertain based on the source dialogue, while a Judge module determines whether the summary meets predefined factual accuracy thresholds. Approved summaries are stored in a PostgreSQL database for downstream clinical integration. Experiments on a synthetic clinical dataset show that CARESUM reaches higher F1 scores in factual accuracy compared to baseline summarization models. These findings demonstrate CARESUM's effectiveness in generating reliable, interpretable, and verifiable clinical summaries, advancing the deployment of trustworthy AI solutions in real-world healthcare environments. © 2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Clinical dialogue summarization; Clinical natural language processing; factual verification; Large Language Models; Retrieval Augmented Generation},
