	affiliations = {Kennesaw State University, Dept. of Computer Science, Marietta, GA, United States},
	abstract = {This paper presents AgentCite, an Agentic AI system designed to autonomously verify information found in documents against their sources. Our work leverages OpenAI’s GPT-4 model and Agents SDK to build the framework. The AgentCite system involves three key components: a Negotiator agent to facilitate communication between parties, a Main Document Agent to access a chosen document, and a Source Documents Agent to access sources referenced in the main document. The workflow is orchestrated through the following steps. First, the system retrieves information from the main document based on a user’s request. Next, it retrieves the same information from the source and analyzes the context. This step is repeated if multiple references are found. Finally, the system concludes whether the information can be verified against the sources and returns its findings to the user. In this paper, we present a case study on a simple document, provide solutions, and discuss the challenges of verification using Large Language Models (LLMs). ©2025 IEEE.},
