	abstract = {The autonomy of users and educated public conversation are seriously threatened by the proliferation of deceptive content on social media platforms. By developing the "AI Manipulation Detector,"a web-based program that can differentiate and reveal persuasive and deceitful language, our project will address this conundrum. Our system uses a hybrid architecture that combines three analytical pillars in a unique way: a revolutionary contextual source analysis module, an adaptive Naive Bayes classifier selected for its interpretability, and a transparent rule-based engine. This integration of text analysis with an author-level "Source Trust Score"is the main contribution'. The first layer of the system is a rule-based engine that looks for verbal cues that point to the possibility of manipulation. This entails recognizing ethically produced manipulative techniques, such as creating a sense of urgency, employing divisive "us versus them"rhetoric, and asserting irrational authority. This gives the analysis a solid and intelligible basis. In order to do contextual source analysis, the second layer communicates with the Reddit API. It determines an author's age and karma to provide a Source Trust Score, which is a crucial component that goes beyond simple text analysis. An adaptive machine learning component makes up the third layer. A Naive Bayes classifier is constructed using a labelled set that can be created with a user feedback system. Model predictions and rule-based scoring are used in the integrated methodology to produce a system that improves its performance over time in an iterative manner. © 2025 IEEE.},
