	affiliations = {Dept. Mechanical Engineering, College of Arts & Information Engineering, Dalian Polytechnic University, Dalian, China; Dept. Liberal Education, College of Arts & Information Engineering, Dalian Polytechnic University, Dalian, China},
	abstract = {To address the dual challenges of high-power grid impact and soaring operational costs at supercharging stations, this study proposes a hierarchical "end-edge-cloud" multi-level coordination framework integrated with multi-time-scale trusted regulation. A realistic 10 kV distribution network model is constructed, incorporating 70 electric vehicles (EVs), 1.6 MW/1.8 MW energy storage systems, and high-penetration wind power. By embedding blockchain-based evidence storage and formal verification into real-time terminal data collection, rapid edge decision-making, and global cloud optimization, a trustworthy closed-loop mechanism of "collect-certify-verify-execute-feedback" is achieved. Rolling optimization across day-ahead and intra-day horizons demonstrates: power deviation within ±2 MW, daily arbitrage revenue of 2,916 CNY via storage-based "valley-charging and peak-discharging", reduced wind curtailment, a 30 % reduction in peak-to-valley load difference, and a total daily operational cost savings of 8,436 CNY. This work not only offers a secure, economical, and verifiable paradigm for large-scale supercharging station operations, but also provides methodological insights for intelligent transportation, distributed energy management, trustworthy AI, and interdisciplinary coordinated control. It advances the deep integration and trustworthy evolution of end-edge-cloud architectures within coupled energy-transportation systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
