	affiliations = {Shanghai Normal University, Tianhua College, Shanghai, China},
	abstract = {As Artificial Intelligence (AI) becomes increasingly embedded in educational practice, understanding how pre-service preschool teachers engage with AI during their professional development is essential. This study examines the relationship between AI literacy and learning engagement in the context of educational internships, with a focus on the mediating role of AI awareness. 202 early childhood education majors from a private college in Shanghai participated in the study, completing a validated questionnaire measuring four dimensions of AI literacy (AI knowledge, AI competence, AI attitude, and AI ethics) alongside AI awareness and learning engagement. Mediation analyses using PROCESS Macro (Model 4) revealed that AI awareness significantly mediated the relationship between each AI literacy component and learning engagement. Specifically, pre-service teachers with higher AI literacy demonstrated greater AI awareness, predicting higher levels of learning engagement during internships. These findings underscore the importance of fostering technical proficiency, critical reflection, and ethical sensitivity toward AI in teacher education programs to enhance engagement and preparedness in digitally transforming educational environments. © 2025 IEEE.},
