	abstract = {This study aims to systematically map the emerging literature on GenAI and Smart Customer Experience Management using bibliometric techniques and clustering published literature. Following the PRISMA framework, 349 peer-reviewed articles were extracted from Scopus and analyzed using VOSviewer. The findings of this study revealed five major clusters: personalization and customer engagement, AI-enabled service automation, AI ethics, biases, and trustworthiness, customer journey orchestration, and AI-driven marketing innovation. Furthermore, it is noted that the majority of publications are from authors based in Western contexts. The literature is fragmented, has limited theoretical lenses, and lacks empirical evidence from emerging markets. This study addresses this gap by proposing a conceptual framework that draws upon Service-Dominant Logic and Technology Acceptance Model literature to theorize the relationship between GenAI mechanisms and value co-creation and customer retention outcomes. It systematically overviews the existing literature, identifies underexplored gaps, and proposes avenues for future empirical research in the emerging markets. © 2025 IEEE},
