	abstract = {This chapter’s conceptual framework focuses on three key pillars: aesthetic leadership, aesthetic dimensions in leaders’ decision processes supported by AI-powered tools, and the balance between AI insights and aesthetic leaders’ judgment in the decision processes. This chapter addresses the following research questions: (1) What dimensions of aesthetic leadership are significant in organisational leaders’ decision processes supported by AI-powered tools? (2) What benefits and risks does the implementation of AI bring to the decision processes of aesthetic leaders? (3) What strategies can be applied to balance AI-based insights and human judgment in aesthetic leaders’ decision processes? The analysis results suggest that leaders’ rational decision models are prioritised in the organisational context. However, aesthetic leaders’ tacit knowledge, including emotional insights, aesthetic considerations that encourage creativity and innovation in organisations, and their holistic perspectives, constitute key factors in aesthetic decision processes. Integrating aesthetic dimensions with leaders’ rational decision models, complemented by real-time data analytics and predictive models from AI machine learning algorithms, natural language processing, and decision support systems, can enhance organisational leaders’ decision-making. Business organisations are working to establish policies that secure a balance between AI-based insights and human judgment in aesthetic leaders’ decision processes. This chapter may bring added value to scholars in leadership and leadership development, AI ethics, organisational aesthetics, as well as business practitioners, leadership trainers and organisational policymakers seeking to integrate in a controlled manner aesthetic dimensions of the decision-making process with AI-powered tools for organisational leaders. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Michał Szostak; individual chapters, the contributors.},
