	affiliations = {Russian University of Transport (MIIT), Moscow, Russian Federation; Pastukhov State Academy of Industrial Management - Branch of the Tomsk State University, Yaroslavl, Russian Federation},
	abstract = {The article is dedicated to the study of emerging competency requirements for graduates in the context of the developing Digital University, which actively integrates artificial intelligence (AI) technologies. The concept of 'centaur' competencies is proposed, implying not just the simple use of AI, but the development of synergistic interaction between humans and machines to solve complex problems. Key components of these competencies are analyzed: critical thinking in the context of AI, AI-enhanced creativity, adaptability, deep digital/AI literacy, and the ethics of AI interaction. Necessary changes in curricula and pedagogical approaches for the purposeful formation of 'centaur' competencies are considered, including project-based learning and the development of skills for customizing AI solutions. The risks of cognitive atrophy due to excessive reliance on AI and strategies to counteract them are discussed. The role of the university in preparing students for the labor market of the sixth technological wave, where human-AI synergy will become the norm of professional activity, is substantiated. © 2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {adaptability; AI ethics; artificial intelligence; centaur competencies; creativity; critical thinking; digital literacy; digital university; future competencies; human-AI synergy; labor market; sixth technological wave},
	keywords = {Commerce; Employment; Engineering education; Students; Teaching; Adaptability; Artificial intelligence ethic; Centaur competency; Creativity; Critical thinking; Digital literacies; Digital university; Future competency; Human-artificial intelligence synergy; Labour market; Sixth technological wave; Artificial intelligence},
