	affiliations = {Vishwakarma Institute of Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering (Artificial Intelligence), Pune, India},
	abstract = {The increasing complexity of social media management brings about major challenges to organizations, including inconsistent standards for content, poor posting schedules, and heavy operational workloads. This study introduces a Generative AI-powered Social Media Automator by combining content creation across various formats with predictive engagement modeling. The framework relies on a dual-layer prompting design: it standardizes the user's intent with a large instruction-following model and then generates text, image, and video materials with Imagen and Phenaki. A YOLOv8-based perception module ensures quality assurance via segmentation, editing, and mistake identification, with human-in-the-loop procedures addressing failures like fabrications and style inconsistencies. For forecasting engagement, we assessed several regression methods on the publicly available Instagram Reach Analysis Data from Kaggle, containing measures such as impressions, reach, likes, comments, shares, and profile visits. Tests revealed that Linear Regression attained the greatest accuracy (R2 = 99.96%), affirming the dataset's pronounced linear nature. Random Forest and Neural Networks also displayed strong performance with R2 values of 89.72% and 90.06%, respectively, whereas KNN yielded adequate outcomes (72.82%), and Decision Tree performed poorly at 44.34%. Charts comparing real versus forecasted engagement further corroborate the results. This comprehensive system not only streamlines content production and planning but also supplies dependable engagement predictions, delivering a functional, expandable, and brand-secure alternative for corporations and small enterprises. © 2025 IEEE.},
