	abstract = {Achieving an optimal balance between performance, interpretability, and regulatory compliance remains a major challenge in data-driven healthcare. To address this, the present study introduces a novel framework that integrates Federated Generative Adversarial Networks (FedGANs) with blockchain technology to enable secure, auditable, and transparent model development. The architecture uniquely combines federated learning for distributed data privacy with blockchain for immutable audit trails and smart contracts that enforce robust access control. In line with the principles of Explainable AI (XAI), the framework incorporates SHAP and LIME to ensure real-time interpretability, thereby enhancing trust and clinical usability. Furthermore, compliance with healthcare regulations such as HL7, FDA, and GDPR is achieved through the system's embedded auditability and security mechanisms. Experimental evaluation on both simulated and real-world healthcare datasets demonstrates that the proposed method preserves confidentiality, transparency, and accountability without compromising predictive accuracy or authenticity. This unified design paves the way for reliable AI deployment in regulated healthcare environments, supporting decision-making that is both explainable and compliant.  © 2025 IEEE.},
