	affiliations = {Vel Tech Rangarajan Dr. Sagunthala R&d Institute of Science and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {The explosion of artificial intelligence in Healthcare (HC) marks the beginning of a new era, a transformative approach that grips the possibility of transforming the domain of patient outcome prediction. KDD for medical data has been widely developed; however, the advancement of heterogeneous medical data sources consisting of both structured (e.g., electronic health records and laboratory outputs) and unstructured data (e.g., Medical records and imaging reports) is still limited. In response, this work presents an AI-based predictive framework that utilizes state-of-the-art data harmonization methods to integrate heterogeneous HC data and improve predictive performance and clinical utility. The proposed approach ensures more reliable and complete patient analysis by tackling the issues associated with traditional systems, such as missing data, inconsistencies, and fragmented data. The framework has shown an order of improvement in predictive outputs referred to with other methods, as measured by Area under the Curve, F-measure, and Mean Absolute Error. Broadly, these results demonstrate the promise that AI-integrated data could have to transform patient intake, providing a cost-effective and reproducible means of supporting outcomes prediction and care trajectories across diverse contexts.  © 2025 IEEE.},
