	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035993002?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Ansys Inc., Design Business Unit (DBU), United States},
	abstract = {As AI-powered applications increasingly migrate to cloud-native infrastructures, ensuring the security of their deployment pipelines has become a critical concern. Kubernetes has emerged as the leading orchestration platform for managing scalable AI workloads; however, its dynamic nature introduces unique challenges for security, governance, and compliance. This paper presents KubeSecOps, a novel framework that provides continuous security assurance in Kubernetes-based DevSecOps pipelines specifically tailored for AI workloads. The proposed architecture integrates policy-as-code enforcement, cryptographic model integrity attestation, runtime threat detection using eBPF, and an adaptive feedback mechanism that evolves policies in real time. Experimental results on real-world AI workloads show that KubeSecOps significantly reduces detection latency, lowers false positive rates, and improves policy enforcement accuracy compared to existing tools such as Falco, StackRox, and SecureMLOps. By embedding security across the full development lifecycle - from code commit to runtime execution - KubeSecOps establishes a scalable, modular, and context-aware defense strategy for trustworthy AI deployments. Baselines were configured for parity; we report mean results with variability, provide minimal ablations to show each layer's contribution, and release sanitized manifests/rules upon acceptance. GPU overhead remains within the throughput drop reported. © 2025 IEEE.},
