	abstract = {The article is devoted to the study of axiological aspects of young people's interaction with digital technologies and artificial intelligence (AI) in the conditions of rapid digitalization of modern society. The authors emphasize that young people, being the main driver and beneficiary of technological innovations, face the need to form new moral and ethical models of using digital services and AI. The article analyzes socio-psychological characteristics of youth, such as increased interest in technology, propensity for quick ethical judgments and susceptibility to mythological narratives, which makes them a key subject in the process of AI adaptation in social life. The authors highlight both positive and negative aspects of young people's interaction with AI. On the one hand, AI has the potential to improve educational processes and increase research efficiency, but on the other hand, it raises concerns about digital dependency, decreased critical thinking, and emotional isolation. Special attention is paid to the phenomenon of "emotional bubbles", when AI companions create an illusion of emotional connection, which can negatively affect the ability to empathy and the formation of moral norms. The article proposes three basic principles of the ideology of interaction with AI: subject-centeredness, transparency and transhumanism. These principles are aimed at ensuring the ethical use of technology, where the human being remains the central subject and AI acts as a tool to improve the quality of life.  © 2025 IEEE.},
