	abstract = {This paper presents the ADAPTIVE-AI framework, a novel approach to enhancing adaptive assessments using Generative AI, Gamification, Instructional Design, and Open Educational Resources (OERs). The framework aims to address key limitations of traditional assessment systems by integrating personalized, AI-driven question generation and dynamic feedback based on real-time learner performance. Additionally, gamification elements, including badges, leaderboards, and rewards, are incorporated to improve learner engagement and motivation. The instructional design component of the framework, grounded in Backward Design and Bloom's Taxonomy, ensures that assessments are aligned with clear learning outcomes, enabling effective measurement of cognitive skills across various levels. The framework also ensures continuous access to relevant educational content through the seamless integration of OERs. By combining instructional design principles, Generative AI, and gamification, the system delivers pedagogically sound, adaptable, and personalized learning assessments. This paper explores the design and potential benefits of the ADAPTIVE-AI framework, emphasizing how AI-driven learning pathways will enable personalized assessments and ensure that the system adapts to the diverse needs of learners across various educational contexts. © 2025 IEEE.},
