	abstract = {In this paper, we propose an Artificial Intelligence (AI) based approach that integrates threat detection, network monitoring, and encryption to establish improved cybersecurity resilience. We utilize the Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS) UNSW-NB15 dataset to introduce AS-BiGCN, an advanced hybrid model that integrates Attention-based Bidirectional Long Short- Term (BiLSTM) and Graph Convolutional Networks (GCN) to learn effective temporal and spatial patterns in network traffic. The attention mechanism increases the significance of features, and the GCN efficiently deals with intricate topological dependencies to enhance the accuracy of intrusion detection. For data confidentiality protection during data transmission, the proposed framework utilizes the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES), which provides powerful protection against unauthorized access. Experimental results show that AS-BiGCN outperforms traditional models in the detection of known and unknown threats with high accuracy, precision, and recall. This comprehensive model offers an extendable and secure solution for real-time network monitoring and safeguarding of sensitive information within a heterogeneous and dynamic network environment. © 2025 IEEE.},
