	abstract = {This concluding part synthesises the volume’s findings, reaffirming the central research problem concerning the transformative impact of AI-powered solutions on the humanistic and aesthetic dimensions of managerial theory and practice. It summarises the answers to this book’s research questions, demonstrating how AI reshapes leadership, decision-making, communication, organisational aesthetics, and human resource practices. The volume highlights the dual potential of AI to foster either humanisation or dehumanisation of work, depending on its aesthetic, ethical, and human-centred implementation. The conclusion emphasises the theoretical and epistemological contributions of integrating humanistic management, organisational aesthetics, and AI ethics while outlining practical recommendations for managers, AI designers, and policymakers. Recognising the conceptual character of many contributions and the Western-centric cultural framing, it also discusses the limitations of the current analyses and proposes directions for future empirical, cross-cultural, and interdisciplinary research. The final reflection advocates for an AI-enhanced management paradigm that safeguards human dignity, emotional depth, and aesthetic richness, ensuring that technological advancement supports the flourishing of individuals within organisations. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Michał Szostak; individual chapters, the contributors.},
