	abstract = {Generative AI’s integration across diverse research domains offers significant advantages. By promising to alleviate dataset biases and safeguard privacy, generative AI holds the potential for fostering more robust and fair research outcomes. However, a notable hurdle emerges from the unequal accessibility of generative AI technology among research institutions. This imbalance exacerbates existing disparities within the research landscape, impeding the equitable progression of knowledge. Furthermore, this challenge is compounded by the recognition that generative AI systems are prone to inadvertently introducing bias and privacy concerns themselves. Consequently, this inadvertently perpetuates and widens inequality, not only within the research community but also in broader society. In addressing these challenges, this chapter aims to thoroughly examine the intricacies associated with applying generative AI in research. Additionally, it endeavors to propose practical solutions and strategies to mitigate these obstacles, thereby fostering a more inclusive and equitable utilization of generative AI technology across various research domains. © The Editors and Contributing Authors Severally 2025. All rights reserved.},
