	abstract = {The inability to interpret decisions made by 'blackbox' AI models remains a primary obstacle to their deployment in building automation, where safety and trust are paramount. To bridge this gap, our work introduces a transparent framework that integrates a low-cost IoT-sensing platform with an interpretable, rule-based decision engine. Our core contributions are an adaptive comfort model using survival analysis and a hierarchical control strategy (Health > Comfort > Energy). The system was deployed over three seasons and the comfort index was increased by 15-18 %, with only a 5.1-8.0 % increase in energy consumption. High ECTI value shows good efficiency, delivering over twice the comfort gain per unit of additional energy consumed. This work establishes a new paradigm for trustworthy, humancentric building automation. © 2025 IEEE.},
