	affiliations = {SRM Institute of Science and Technology, Kattankulathur, Faculty of Engineering and Technology, Department of Data Science and Business Systems, School of Computing, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India; Gitam Deemed-to-be University, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Bangalore, 561203, India},
	abstract = {In recent years, generative artificial intelligence (AI) models have demonstrated exceptional capabilities in producing human-like responses in various domains, including healthcare, and are increasingly being adopted in mission-critical systems, necessitating integration of security resilient architecture [1]. However, the adoption of these models in sensitive medical settings raises significant concerns about data privacy, security, and explainability. This paper presents SecGenAI, a securityintegrated generative AI model designed for privacy-preserving and explainable health chatbot interactions. SecGenAI integrates fine-tuned Generative Pre-trained Transformer 2 (GPT2)/Biomedical GPT (BioGPT) with 1) Advanced Encryption Standard (AES)256 encryption (8.3 ∼ m s latency), 2) Opacuspowered differential privacy, and 3) clinician-validated explainability (78 % interpretability score). Experiment shows 6% attack success (vs. 41 % baseline) while maintaining 4.2/5 medical accuracy. The proposed architecture ensures encrypted communication, secure model training, and transparent response generation, making it suitable for deployment in real-world clinical environments. Evaluation metrics and experimental results validate the effectiveness of our approach in maintaining both data integrity and conversational quality.  © 2025 IEEE.},
