	abstract = {An explosion in the amount of data being created at the edge of the network and mounting demands on network latency, privacy, and bandwidth inflexibility compel us to rethink the underlying structure of the AI infrastructure. Conventional cloud-driven architectures tend to be inefficient in real-time, privacy-conscientious and bandwidth-saving AI software. This paper proposes Cloudless AI, a new paradigm that reinvents the vision of AI infrastructure through a decentralized perspective, edge-first. Our architecture can easily scale due to the use of federated learning, lightweight compression of the model, and the edge-native orchestration framework to build a scalable, secure and responsive AI deployment on heterogeneous edge devices. The system architecture is answering important concerns such as what to do with data that need to be handled in a decentralized manner, having a heterogeneous set of processors and where there is connectivity all the time. Experimental analyses show that inferences in benchmark datasets are much faster, conserve power, and are much more secure than similar inferences in the more traditional cloud-based methods. The suggested Cloudless AI triggers a feasible direction to democratize AI abilities and guarantee the sustained strength, flexibility, and alignment with the new data governance approaches.  © 2025 IEEE.},
