	abstract = {In the digital age, data has become a powerful and renewable form of capital, yet its benefits remain concentrated among corporations and state actors. This paper aims to present Webfare as a transformative model that redistributes data wealth, prioritising ethical, equitable, and sustainable use for societal wellbeing. This framework empowers individuals, institutions, and communities to reclaim, manage, and capitalise on their data assets, moving beyond traditional welfare models. By integrating data cooperatives, synthetic data generation, and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Artificial Intelligence (AI) models, Webfare ensures privacy, fairness, and responsible AI deployment. It promotes a circular data economy, where data is not just a tool for private profit but a public good, reinvested into social progress. Ultimately, Webfare redefines data ownership and AI’s role in society, fostering economic efficiency, social equity, ethical governance, and democratic empowerment – building a future where data serves the many, not just the few. © Rosenberg & Sellier.},
