	affiliations = {Effat University, College of Engineering, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia},
	abstract = {Powerline Communication (PLC) systems are critical for smart infrastructure, but their reliability is severely hindered by persistent security vulnerabilities and non-stationary signal interference. Traditional, static security and optimization methods fail to adapt to these dynamic challenges. This paper proposes, implements, and validates via simulation a novel, integrated Artificial Intelligence (AI) framework designed to enhance both the security and performance of PLC networks simultaneously. The framework leverages a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) network for real-time Intrusion Detection System (IDS) and a Q-Learning Reinforcement Learning (RL) agent for adaptive channel and transmission optimization. The system is evaluated in a detailed simulated PLC environment modeling frequency-selective channel attenuation and complex impulsive noise. Simulation results demonstrate the LSTM-IDS achieving a high detection accuracy of 95.3% for identifying anomalous traffic. Furthermore, the Q-Learning agent successfully adapts to noise fluctuations, reducing the average packet loss rate by 42% and improving the Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR) by over 18 dB compared to a static baseline. This work provides an original, quantitative validation of an integrated AI approach, proving its potential to transform PLC into a robust, self-optimizing, and secure communication technology.  © 2025 IEEE.},
