	abstract = {Free speech is a foundational axiom of democracy. The era of digitalization facilitates free speech through various social media platforms. However, the technological revolution has seen a proliferation of hate speech, misinformation and cyber threats. In contemporary times, artificial intelligence (AI) algorithms are being used for content moderation to restrain the dissemination of hate speech. The algorithms act as a double-edged sword and pose a digital conundrum for democratic societies in balancing free speech and hate speech. This chapter explores the dynamic interface between free speech, hate speech and algorithms-based restrictions in democratic societies particularly in India. It examines the legislative measures in India that are reliant on auto-censorship and the challenges it poses concerning free speech. By integrating the civil society critique and judicial oversight, the chapter attempts to provide holistic overview of algorithmic content moderation. The chapter highlights ethical AI regulation policies across the world at the end. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Pallavi Devi and Alankar Kaushik; individual chapters, the contributors. All rights reserved.},
