	affiliations = {B.S. Abdur Rahman Crescent Institute of Science and Technology, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {Artificial intelligence (AI) plays a crucial role in processing vast amounts of medical data from digital health records and health-tracking devices. In Asia-Pacific and Europe, digital healthcare and citizen empowerment are reshaping healthcare systems, underpinned by international guidelines ensuring trustworthy AI in medical imaging for enhanced diagnostics and treatments. Alongside this, digital twins integration emerges as a pivotal trend, employing advanced AI algorithms to enhance predictive models. A digital twin represents a real-time, comprehensive model of a physical asset, capturing current status and historical data. This technology plays a crucial role in assessing conditions, predicting behaviors, and optimizing operations within healthcare settings. Furthermore, as telemedicine advances with big data and IoT, innovative health solutions for remote monitoring are increasingly reliant on digital twins, necessitating stringent data protection and ethical standards. This survey paper explores the transformative impact of AI and digital twins on modern healthcare, emphasizing their role in improving efficiency and patient outcomes. © 2025 Elsevier Inc. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.},
