	abstract = {Public relations practitioners have a vital role in helping to make artificial intelligence (AI) more transparent to their organizations’ stakeholders. AI tools are becoming increasingly sophisticated; thus, AI and its applications are becoming far more difficult for laypeople to understand. Furthermore, many AI components are being deliberately kept secret. The efforts of public relations practitioners to make AI more transparent could also help clarify existing misperceptions about AI’s capabilities. Furthermore, practitioners’ efforts to increase transparency would help to identify and to rectify AI’s potential for abuse. Although AI tools and their applications have sparked people’s imaginations throughout the world, the limitations of AI must also be fully recognized both by organizations’ publics as well as by society at large. Public relations practitioners can provide a valuable service to their publics and to global society at large by accurately, fairly, and comprehensively communicating AI’s limitations and its inherent dangers, and by helping to clarify existing misconceptions and misunderstanding about AI technology. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Regina Luttrell and Adrienne A. Wallace; individual chapters, the contributors.},
