	abstract = {Today's fast evolving technological landscape doesn't let even the most traditional of machine learning models keep up with data streams that are evolving rapidly on real time, leading to higher level of inaccuracy and something that is no longer relevant, whether it is about healthcare, finance or smart cities. Such models are needlessly restricted by not being scalable, and not adaptible due to the demands for constant human intervention to retune and optimize them. To overcome this problem, we introduce a Dynamic, Self Evolving AI (DSAI) framework that will allow of the creation, optimization, and improvement of machine leaning models autonomously on a real time basis without assistance from humans. Meta learning algorithms, continuous data stream integration, as well as reinforcement learning are used in DSAI framework to continuously evolve models based on the changing conditions and to continuously improve their performance. The system provides fair and related outcomes through the use of ethical guardrails and real time feedback mechanisms for widespread applications. This self driving framework reduces the need for manual updates, and therefore increases model accuracy, and helps in providing scalable solutions in the industries with high speed. Finally, with DSAI, we have an approach to machine learning which is sustainable and adaptive enough to handle real time as well as the challenges in a long run, gearing well to an increasingly data driven environment. © 2025 IEEE.},
