	abstract = {The way healthcare has been practiced has changed considerably, from traditional ages-old methods to modern technology led approaches. At the core of this revolution is artificial intelligence (AI), which is transforming healthcare by improving diagnoses, tailoring and personalizing treatment, and improving hospital operations. AI techniques, such as machine learning, deep learning, and natural language processing, are being used in various segments, such as medical imaging, predictive analytics, drug discovery, robotic surgery, and managing patient care. These advancements make it possible to detect diseases at an early stage, customize drugs according to genetic diagnosis, and increase the accessibility of medical care, particularly in underserved regions. Despite significant potential, the implementation of AI in healthcare faces numerous issues pertaining to biased algorithms, data privacy, and ethical responsibility, as well as the lack of regulatory requirements in place. It is imperative to address these issues to ensure fair, safe, and effective use of AI. The chapter also observes future directions, such as the AI and blockchain fused for secure data handling and AI wearable in preventive healthcare. Moving forward, AI will continue to radically change the management of global health, from personalized medicine to response to epidemics. The involvement of the coalition of healthcare professionals, the technologists, and policy makers will be imperative to help AI stay in check the way it ought so that it becomes a valuable contributor to patient outcomes and the efficiency of the healthcare systems across the globe. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved..},
