	affiliations = {Bharati Vidyapeeth's Institute Of Computer Applications And Management(BVICAM), New Delhi, India; Lovely Professional University, Dept. Of Library And Information Science, Jalandhar, India; Lovely Professional University, Dept. Of Punjabi, Jalandhar, India},
	abstract = {This study examines the usage patterns, advantages, and limitations of Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools among university faculties in India. A survey of 400 participants from various academic disciplines was conducted to assess their awareness of AI tools, their usage, purposes, benefits, and barriers. The collected data were analyzed using statistical software (SPSS). The findings suggest that the 92 % of faculty members have aware of AI tools, and 76 % faculty members actively use of it in some form. The majority of the top tools were plagiarism checkers (84 %), reference managers (74 %), and writing assistants (68 %), which primarily support research publication. Faculty from Clinical and STEM disciplines used AI tools less frequently for early-stage research tasks such as data analysis (54%) and literature review (48%). The key advantages reported included faster writing (72 %), higher publication quality (61 %), and reduced time spent on data analysis (58 %), indicating that AI enhances both productivity and research quality. The main challenge identified, revealed by 45 % of respondents, was a lack of training. Although AI adoption is increasing, the study finds limited integration of A I in advanced analytical and exploratory research stages. To realize AI's full potential, educational institutions should invest in ethical governance, curriculum integration, collaborative research networks, equitable access to advanced infrastructure, and training on AI ethics and literacy. Furthermore, research relevance and inclusivity can be enhanced by developing localized AI solutions tailored to India's linguistic and cultural diversity. Overall, it can be said that the advent of artificial intelligence shows significant potential to enhance productivity and foster creativity in the field of research, as well as strengthen the global position of Indian academia. © 2025 IEEE.},
