	abstract = {The rapid rise of Generative AI is reshaping higher education, prompting higher education institutions (HEIs) to review their AI strategies. This study offers an early examination of how university administrations are navigating these AI-driven transformations. Based on semi-structured interviews with eight administrative leaders and faculty members, the findings reveal the shifting responsibilities AI brings to administrative leaders and the growing need for the university community to develop AI literacy. Participants consistently cited key challenges, including limited resources, fragmented AI initiatives, and the absence of a unified leadership vision. As AI continues to influence educational formats and content, sustainable implementation will require HEIs to prepare students with future-ready skills, foster meaningful community engagement, and leverage internal institutional expertise in AI. Despite overall positive attitudes, participants also have concerns about how AI may reshape the core values of education. These early insights offer a foundation for future research and policy development about AI in education. © 2025 IEEE.},
