	affiliations = {Department of CSE-UIE, Chandigarh University, Mohali, India; Advanced Centre of Research and Innovation (ACRI), Department of Computer Science & Engineering CGC, Punjab, Jhanjeri, India},
	abstract = {While its origins date back to manufacturing, machine learning (ML) is transforming a range of industries. It has already transformed the banking, agriculture, healthcare, education, and urban planning sectors. It has been used in manufacturing for many years in predictive maintenance, quality control, and process automation. Now, ML facilitates data-driven decision-making, intelligent automation, and operational effectiveness across an array of fields. Big data, deep learning, reinforcement learning, and generative AI have all come together to accelerate the uptake of ML, which assists companies and organizations in enhancing processes, productivity, and solutions that were not possible before. Besides enhancing algorithmic trading, risk assessment, and fraud detection in the financial sector, ML also enhances drug research, medical imaging, and disease diagnosis in the healthcare sector. ML is applied in precision agriculture, intelligent urban planning, and adaptive educational systems to advance increased sustainability, efficiency, and decision-making. As ML becomes more ingrained in business operations, concerns including data privacy, model interpretability, and ethical AI governance need to be addressed to guarantee responsible deployment. This chapter looks at the various applications, strategies, challenges, and future directions of ML in a variety of industries. People will have a comprehensive understanding of how ML is transforming traditional processes, fostering digital transformation, fostering intelligent automation, and enhancing people's lives globally by taking into account real-world case studies and innovations from specific industries. © 2026 selection and editorial matter, Nishant Ranjan, Rashi Tyagi, Ranvijay Kumar, Ashutosh Tripathi, and Amit Verma; individual chapters, the contributors.},
