	abstract = {It seems that the widespread use of artificial intelligence (AI) in the healthcare sector is rapidly growing. In the upcoming years, AI-driven healthcare is expected to grow rapidly, according to economic analysts. This exponential expansion has given rise to several problems. It is crucial to look at the privacy, security, and ethical aspects of AI systems to prevent unintentional negative consequences and hazards associated with using AI in healthcare. This chapter will discuss the ethical, security, patient consent, and privacy issues that AI in healthcare raises and will provide solutions. It will also stress the need for the benefits of an AI-driven healthcare system. To address ethical difficulties, the article presents ethical considerations, ethical AI frameworks, regulatory frameworks, and policy proposals. It highlights how crucial it is to strike a balance between innovation and moral issues to defend patient rights and preserve public confidence in the healthcare system. To develop ethical norms, challenges, and future directions that are in line with technological improvements in healthcare, the study promotes further research and stakeholder interaction. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Rakesh Kumar and Meenu Gupta individual chapters, the contributors.},
