	abstract = {This research proposes a high-precision ontology-driven AI framework for automating legal reasoning, contract lifecycle management, and intelligent dispute resolution in commercial law. By integrating formal legal ontologies (e.g., OWL, LegalRuleML) with transformer-based NLP models, SPIN constraints, and SWRL rule engines, the system achieves scalable, explainable, and regulation-aligned legal automation. Evaluated on a corpus of over 220,000 commercial legal documents - including procurement contracts, lease agreements, insurance policies, and service-level agreements - the framework consistently delivered clause classification accuracies above 94.6% and F1-scores reaching 0.94. Reasoning fidelity and compliance scores were above 0.95, verifying strong legal logic and regulatory compliance. The system proposed in this work outperformed baseline models with accuracy gains of 5.3%-5.6% and up to 61% reduction of manual review time for contracts. Semantic transparency was ensured by SHACL-based validation, clause-to-rule mapping, and XAI feature analysis, providing end-to-end auditable legal analytics. With a less than 1.3 second average runtime latency, and multi-jurisdictional flexibility without the need to modify architecture, the framework is ready for real-world use in enterprise-level legal tech platforms to identify risks, ensure compliance, and enable computer-assisted legal decision-making.  © 2025 IEEE.},
