	abstract = {The exponential growth of user-generated content on social media has raised the need for automated moderation systems that are dependable, scalable, and objective. AI-driven solutions are necessary because offensive images and dangerous text usually evade manual review. This paper presents a multimodal moderation framework that integrates Hugging Face Transformers with Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers (BERT) for textual analysis and a Vision Transformer (ViT) for visual evaluation. We use pre-trained Hugging Face models for both text and image content moderation, which have been refined on benchmark datasets for offensive language and inappropriate imagery, in contrast to the majority of previous works that rely on custom architectures or unimodal pipelines.Using developments in image-text reasoning, meme classification, and hate speech detection, the combination of linguistic and visual embeddings allows for more reliable identification of content that violates policies. Using Hugging Face's ecosystem for scalable and reproducible content moderation is effective, as evidenced by experimental results showing that this multimodal framework performs noticeably better than unimodal baselines in terms of accuracy and F1-score. © 2025 IEEE.},
