	abstract = {Modern ICT applications increasingly demand intelligent edge computing solutions that prioritize user privacy and operational independence. This paper presents an innovative edge-based multimodal framework designed for enhanced human-computer interaction, specifically targeting accessibility enhancement applications. The proposed architecture integrates models of computer vision algorithms, natural language processing, and speech synthesis technologies within a compact embedded computing environment. Utilizing advanced deep learning models including YOLOv8 for real-time visual analysis, Tesseract for document processing, and VOSK for speech interpretation, the framework demonstrates comprehensive multimodal capabilities while maintaining complete operational autonomy. The system achieves application-specific performance targets: 850ms for object detection, 1240ms for OCR, and 980ms for face recognition, making it suitable for environmental awareness and social interaction scenarios. Novel optimization strategies including dynamic quantization (23-31% inference time reduction) and priority-based scheduling enable effective multimodal AI execution on resource-constrained hardware. The system architecture emphasizes resource optimization strategies specifically designed for constrained hardware environments, making it suitable for widespread deployment in diverse ICT applications where privacy preservation and offline functionality are paramount. © 2025 IEEE.},
