	abstract = {The article explores the evolution of educational needs and necessary competencies for students amidst the rapid development of artificial intelligence (AI) and the emergence of the Digital University. It analyzes the transition from the paradigm of teaching the use of AI as a tool to developing students' ability to act as co-creators, critical evaluators, and ethical navigators in a world saturated with intelligent systems. Key didactic tasks are considered: developing deep AI literacy, including understanding the fundamental principles, classifications, parameters, and limitations of AI; forming 'centaur' competencies for synergistic interaction with AI; teaching the basics of prompt engineering and customization of AI solutions; instilling skills of ethical reflection, understanding legal aspects, and responsible application of AI; as well as preparing for lifelong learning in the context of constantly evolving AI technologies. Futuristic aspects of further AI integration into education and life, and the corresponding challenges for educational programs, including the need to develop promising research directions, are discussed. © 2025 IEEE.},
