	affiliations = {Saveetha School of Engineering, Saveetha Institute of Medical and Technical Sciences, Simats, Saveetha University, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {Autonomous Vehicles (AVs) are at the forefront of intelligent transportation systems, requiring robust and adaptive decision-making capabilities to navigate complex and dynamic environments. While Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) has demonstrated promising results in optimizing autonomous driving policies through continuous learning, its opaque decision-making process poses significant challenges in terms of trust, safety, and regulatory compliance. This study proposes a novel framework that integrates Explainable AI (XAI) with DRL to bridge the gap between high-performance autonomous control and interpretability. The proposed system enables real-time transparency by offering visual and semantic explanations for driving actions, policy decisions, and environmental interactions. Through simulation in high-fidelity driving environments and evaluation on real-world datasets, the model demonstrates improved policy interpretability, safe exploration, and user trust without compromising performance. This approach addresses a critical need for explainable autonomy paving the way for the deployment of accountable and human-understandable AI systems in next-generation self-driving vehicles. © 2025 IEEE.},
