	abstract = {Healthcare data contains highly sensitive information, making privacy a top priority in AI-based medical systems. Traditional centralized machine learning aggregates data from multiple sources, raising concerns about privacy breaches, data ownership, and regulatory compliance. Federated Learning (FL) offers a solution by allowing AI models to be trained across decentralized data sources without moving patient data. Only model updates are shared, preserving privacy. FL uses tools like differential privacy and secure multi-party computation to enhance security. Algorithms such as FedAvg and FedProx enable collaborative training without exposing individual data. FL also supports IoMT devices, allowing them to contribute to model training while keeping data local. This not only safeguards patient privacy but also addresses the challenge of limited, diverse medical data across institutions. Federated Learning helps build secure, compliant, and flexible AI systems in healthcare, ensuring both innovation and protection of sensitive patient information. © 2025 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.},
