	abstract = {Mobile computing and intelligence are advancing the nature of modern technology by integrating mobility, connectivity and intelligence with the capability of processing real-time data with help of artificial intelligence (AI). This survey aims to discuss development, current status, and future direction of mobile systems with AI integration. Some of these are NPUs, light-weigh AI frameworks, and AI's interaction with the 5G network. Such innovations make smart applications including personal assistants, health monitoring, smart city infrastructure, and gaming. The paper identifies key issues, which are energy efficiency, data management, computational limitation, and ethics, which include bias in the AI model. New trends, including federated learning, edge computing and multimodal AI systems are discussed as the potential ways to overcome these challenges and improve UX and security. As the future direction, the focus is made on the possibilities of the 6G networks, the AI preserving the privacy, and the development of mobile AI both hardware and software. Mobile computing and intelligence are promising to propel innovation in industries, enhance human's welfare, and advance sustainable development of technology. Which is why this survey is important in defining the future where mobile intelligent systems are part of daily life. © 2025 IEEE.},
