	abstract = {This study investigates how AI-ethical design factors influence organizational sustainable performance through the mediating roles of employee digital well-being and Green Human Resource Management (GHRM) outcomes. Drawing on AMO theory and socio-technical systems theory, a cross-sectional survey was conducted, with 550 responses collected and 509 valid samples analyzed using Partial Least Squares Structural Equation Modeling (PLSSEM). The results demonstrate that ethical AI design enhances employee digital well-being, which positively drives GHRM outcomes and, in turn, strengthens sustainable organizational performance. Mediation analyses further confirm sequential pathways linking AI ethics, well-being, and GHRM practices to sustainability. The findings extend existing HRM and AI ethics literature by integrating digital well-being into the GHRM-sustainability nexus, while providing practical guidance for managers to embed ethical AI principles, foster employee well-being, and institutionalize sustainability-focused HRM practices. Keywords: Artificial Intelligence, Ethical AI, Green HRM, Digital Well-being, Sustainability © 2025 IEEE.},
