	abstract = {The article explores the role of EU to foster digital cooperation in the Indo-Pacific region, with particular focus on Southeast Asian region, from the perspective of strategic docking. Against the background of the emerging strategic importance of Indo-Pacific and the closer EU-ASEAN relations, this paper aims to navigate the role played by the EU in shaping the digital governance in the region, assess the strategic value of enhanced cooperation in the field of digital connectivity, and examine the possible benefits and challenges it entails. Using the concept of strategic docking, this chapter analyzes how the EU’s position on digital governance aligns with that of ASEAN, both from conceptual and policy perspectives, and examines the implications for EU-ASEAN relations. It investigates the digital influences the EU can bring to the Southeast Asian region and the strategic benefits of a joint EU-ASEAN approach to digital governance and explores the implications for building the region’s digital order. In order to tackle the questions, the research applies qualitative research method with desk research as a main focus, plus the content analysis of the major policy documents from both sides to explore the potentiality of establishing digital cooperative partnership between them. © 2025 The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd..},
