	abstract = {Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence (HCAI) in virtual assistants enhances user interactions by fostering seamless communication between humans and machines. By integrating advanced AI algorithms and emotional intelligence, virtual assistants can understand user emotions, preferences, and behavior, ensuring more personalized and meaningful interactions. This approach prioritizes user needs, ethical AI principles, and transparency, allowing AI systems to respond effectively while maintaining human oversight. Ethical considerations in HCAI emphasize fairness, accountability, and data privacy, ensuring that AI-driven decisions are unbiased, explainable, and respectful of user autonomy. Through continuous training and adaptive learning, HCAI-driven virtual assistants aim to achieve the highest level of user satisfaction by providing context-aware, emotionally intelligent, and privacy-preserving responses while adhering to responsible AI development practices. This study compares Google Assistant and Siri using realworld queries and integrates OpenAI's Whisper for multilingual speech recognition. The setup evaluates accuracy and contextual understanding across English, Tamil, and Malayalam, highlighting the need for ethical, emotionallyaware AI systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
