	abstract = {The LegalInsights-AI framework presents a hybrid deep learning and machine learning approach to evaluating judicial decisions under the Criminal Procedure Act, 2022 in India's justice system. This model integrates Legal-BERT, Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks, and an ensemble of Random Forest and XGBoost classifiers to assess procedural compliance, identify misapplications of legal provisions, and analyze case outcomes. The framework was trained and validated on a diverse dataset comprising Supreme Court, High Court, and District Court rulings. Experimental results demonstrate that LegalInsights-AI achieves an accuracy of 96.59%, significantly outperforming traditional NLP techniques and rule-based models. The model effectively detects procedural compliance in 80% of analyzed cases, identifies misapplications in 25.9% of cases, and provides a time reduction of 81.2% in case analysis compared to human legal review. Furthermore, the AI model closely aligns with expert legal assessments, achieving a 93.2% match in procedural compliance detection and 91.5% in legal provision application accuracy. These results indicate the potential of LegalInsights-AI to improve judicial transparency, optimize case evaluations, and assist legal professionals in ensuring procedural fairness. Future work will focus on enhancing interpretability, expanding datasets, and integrating explainable AI (XAI) techniques to further refine legal compliance analysis. © 2025 IEEE.},
