	affiliations = {School of Computer Engineering, KIIT Deemed to be University, Bhubaneswar, India; Dr. Sudhir Chandra Sur Institute of Technology and Sports Complex, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Kolkata, India},
	abstract = {Parkinson's disease (PD) is a progressive neuro-degenerative condition with an urgent need for timely and pinpoint diagnosis for adequate treatment. Despite potential for prediction with traditional machine learning techniques, PD data remains difficult to solve for traditional machine learning techniques due to the high computational complexity and the nature of data. We introduce in this work a Hybrid Quantum-Classical AI Framework that combines advantages of QC and provide benefits in predictive accuracy as well as computational efficiency for real time Parkinson's disease detection. We use classical deep learning models in conjunction with Variational Quantum Circuits (VQC) to perform efficient feature extraction and classification of biomedical signals: speech and its recordings, gait analysis, and EEG data. We evaluate the performance of our proposed framework against deep learning models that are standard and based on the accuracy, precision, recall and processing time. Our experimental results suggest that our hybrid quantum classical model outperforms classical methods for both accuracy and efficiency, demonstrating the potential of quantum machine learning (QML) in healthcare. This work gives a taste of the quantum revolution realized in medical diagnostics and paves the way for what could in the future be quantum enhanced disease prediction. © 2025 IEEE.},
