	affiliations = {Genpact, Data Science & Insights, Banglore, India},
	abstract = {Claims processing remains one of the most important business processes in an insurance company as it has a great influence on the customer experience. However, these methods are often labor-intensive and prone to inconsistencies which makes the case for an automated and more efficient system very strong. The aim is to provide a low-cost automation solution for processing insurance claims. This study presents a new approach to claims handling by proposing a data-based framework powered by Generative AI (GenAI) that aims to improve the efficiency of claims handling processes. The proposal includes the automated transformation of email into structured JSON, the extraction of relevant entities from claims, and the automatic verdict generation with (approvals/rejections) and comprehensive, understandable justification remarks. The framework uses Phi-3.5, optimized through Quantized Low-Rank Adaptation (QLoRA), for computational efficiency and scalability. To train the model effectively, we generated a synthetic dataset using multiple large language models (LLMs). This helped the model understand different writing styles and real-world variations, leading to 98% accuracy in entity extraction and 99.63% in verdict generation. Beyond accuracy, the framework follows Responsible AI (RAI) principles, ensuring fair and transparent decision-making while reducing financial risks. © 2025 IEEE.},
