	affiliations = {Birla Institute of Technology and Science, Department of Computer Science, Dubai, United Arab Emirates},
	abstract = {Automated hiring systems, powered by machine learning, are increasingly adopted by organizations to streamline candidate selection. However, these systems risk perpetuating and amplifying historical biases, particularly concerning gender and race. This study presents FairHire, a fairness-aware hiring framework that detects and mitigates bias in resume screening models. A baseline model (Random Forest) was trained using a curated resume dataset, evaluated, and subjected to bias analysis. Fairness metrics including Demographic Parity Difference and Equalized Odds Difference were computed using Fairlearn. Mitigation strategies were then applied to reduce bias in the sensitive attributes. Results demonstrate that fairness constraints can substantially reduce bias when applied during model training. The study highlights the importance of incorporating fairness into AI-based hiring workflows and provides a practical framework for hiring and other decision-making applications.  © 2025 IEEE.},
