	affiliations = {Bharathi Women's College (Autonomous), Department of Computer Science, Tamil Nadu, Chennai, India; Swarnandhra College of Engineering and Technology, Department of MCA, India; Rajalakshmi Engineering College, Department of ECE, Chennai, India; Islamic Banks, Zarqa University, Faculty of Economics and Administrative Sciences, Zarqa, Jordan; University of Business and Technology, College of Business Administration, Jeddah, 21448, Saudi Arabia; Lovely Professional University, School of Electronics and Electrical Engineering, Phagwara, India; Saveetha Institute of Medical and Technical Sciences (SIMATS), Saveetha School of Engineering, Saveetha University, Department of VLSI Microelectronics, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {Blockchain technology and deep learning are converging to offer new means of building AI systems that are powerful and efficient as well as ethical, secure, and transparent. The decentralized, immutable and tamper-proof characteristics of blockchain mitigate many of the challenges that exist in deep learning, including data privacy, trust, and accountability. Deep learning, on the other hand, provides us with robust computational techniques for identifying tight relationships within massive datasets, which elevates the predictive power of AI systems. To overcome the challenges in information security, privacy, transparency, and ethical decision-making in AI, this study proposes new techniques of synergy between blockchain and deep learning AI. Some of the critical aspects of this integration are the usage of blockchain to create a verifiable audit trail of the AI model training process, data provenance, and enabling secure energyefficient sharing of data between distributed entities. In this comprehensive study, latest findings on new areas on the Confines of Blockchain & deep learning applied to AI systems are reviewed and discussed along with how the mutual complementing security aspects of each other can be providing the solutions to the risk/metrology challenges faced in AI. In addition, blockchain's consensus mechanisms, smart contracts, and decentralized frameworks are investigated as tools to improve the transparency and fairness of AI decisionmaking processes. It also explored the combination of blockchain with federated learning, which allows the decentralized and privacy-preserving training of AI models, while maintaining the integrity of the training data. This study shows how the combination of blockchain and deep learning appears successful in constructing more ethical and trustworthy AI systems after a comprehensive review of the literature concerning existing implementations and case studies. By integrating blockchain with deep learning, the research tries to augment security and data integrity, besides addressing bigger ethical issues like accountability for AI decision making and potential data monopolization issues. This study ends with a consideration of the possible challenges to this integration, such as scalability, energy consumption and regulatory implications, and also proposes avenues for future research to improve the integration of blockchain technology with the IoT.  © 2025 IEEE.},
