	affiliations = {Institute of Communication and Computer Systems, Athens, Greece; Institute of Communication and Computer Systems, Athens University of Economics and Business, Athens, Greece; National Technical University of Athens, Athens, Greece},
	abstract = {The growing demand for transparency, accountability, and reproducibility in artificial intelligence (AI) has uncovered significant gaps in current documentation and knowledge management practices. While recent efforts such as Model Cards and Data Cards provide structured documentation for static artifacts, they do not manage to sufficiently capture the dynamic and iterative nature of AI experimentation. Furthermore, the importance of reutilizing the knowledge of previously conducted experiments can often be neglected. In this paper, we introduce Experiment Cards, a novel knowledge management and documentation framework for reproducible AI design and development. The proposed framework integrates automatically captured metadata with human-in-the-loop feedback, documenting essential experimentation-driven aspects, including intent, constraints, evaluation metrics, and lessons learnt. Furthermore, to promote interoperability and alignment with software engineering standards, Experiment Cards are exportable in JSON-LD format and embed semantics from MLCommons CROISSANT data cards and Hugging Face model card schemas. The framework is scheduled to be evaluated through pilots across various use cases, spanning from mobility to industry to evaluate its usability and scalability in real-world settings. © 2025 IEEE.},
