	abstract = {As Artificial Intelligence (AI) becomes more prevalent in business, concerns about its environmental impact grow. Despite its significant carbon footprint, AI also promises to foster sustainability. This chapter explores the relationship between strategic AI focus in business and its environmental effects. Using industry insights and data analysis, we examine metrics like emissions, resource utilization, and environmental innovation. Our main finding is that AI is widely applied to maximize efficiency in production and operations for profit. A side effect is a positive association between a firm’s strategic AI focus and emissions performance. However, AI focus is not significantly linked to resource use and environmental innovation. While AI focus may indicate visionary leadership, it is often applied with a short-term mindset. This chapter highlights ethical and sustainability considerations, calling for more ambitious and responsible AI utilization. © The Editor and Contributors Severally 2025.},
