	abstract = {Over the past few decades, artificial intelligence (AI) integration into marketing strategy (MS) has evolved significantly. Initially conceptualized in the 1950s, AI began transforming marketing practices in the late 1990s and early 2000s, with substantial advancements in the 2010s due to machine learning (ML), and Deep Learning (DL), algorithms within Big Data Analytics. This study consists of a Systematic Literature Review (SLR) examining the current state and future trends of AI applications in MS. A total of 238 articles published in 92 journals were selected from eight reputable databases (i.e., Scopus, Springer Link, Taylor & Francis, Emerald Insight, Sage Pub, Wiley, IEEE, MDPI), using a rigorous research nomenclature. The findings highlight six key areas where AI impacts MS: 1) Performance Measurement and Analytics; 2) Automation; 3) Personalization and Targeting; 4) Customer Segmentation; 5) Positioning and Branding; and 6) Ethics on Customer Privacy. AI enhances operational efficiency, personalization, and strategic optimization, but ethical concerns remain regarding data privacy and security. Future trends indicate promising advancements in predictive analytics, personalization, and the integration of AI with augmented and virtual reality (AR/VR). Meanwhile, ensuring transparent and responsible AI use is crucial for maintaining consumer trust and achieving sustainable marketing success. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Hannah D. Walters and Rachel M. Hammond; individual chapters, the contributors.},
