	abstract = {Artificial Intelligence (AI) is changing the landscape of academic research by facilitating tools and techniques that improve various stages of the research process. The addition of AI into academic research enhances research methodologies by improving data collection and analysis, enabling researchers to expose insights more efficiently. AI contributes to an innovative research environment by automating routine tasks and offering predictive capabilities. AI tools are assisting assist in organizing vast amounts of data, identifying trends, literature review, and data analysis, hence improving the overall quality of research output. This paper portrays the transformative role of AI in academic research by exploring its application across various stages of the research workflow. This study reports the use of AI for data analysis, and model construction, offering researchers more accuracy and speed than traditional methods. Furthermore, the paper introduces the development of a Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen AI) application to interact with PDF documents. This AI-driven app facilitates researchers to engage in conversational interactions with academic texts, thereby simplifying the process of extracting key information. The GenAI app is developed using open-source tools including Google Colab, the HuggingFace model, and the Langchain Framework. This application demonstrates the practical potential of AI in improving knowledge discovery in research. The research is extended by incorporating experiments conducted using Google AI Studio, a platform that offers robust generative AI capabilities. The study concludes by highlighting AI's influence on academic research, anticipating how it will continue to reshape research practices in the future. As AI and GenAI advance, lead to more interdisciplinary collaboration and innovations in academic research.  © 2025 IEEE.},
