	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ResgenXAI64788.2025.11344022},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105033533543?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {The accelerating integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML) marks a fundamental redefinition within the global financial landscape. This paper introduces a capability maturity model for AI adoption in financial institutions and a cross-functional mapping of algorithmic risk factors. We systematically examine the pervasive influence of AI and ML across key segments including retail banking, wealth management, corporate banking, and the evolving payment ecosystem. Through use-case analyses, we demonstrate how advanced computational paradigms are enhancing predictive analytics, fraud detection, and client personalization. The paper also synthesizes the strategic imperatives and ethical considerations for responsible AI deployment, while offering a forward-looking perspective on how AI is shaping future operational models in finance. © 2025 IEEE.},
