	abstract = {Since its founding in the early 1970s, EDPACS: The EDP Audit, Control, and Security Newsletter has provided practitioners with practical insights on IT auditing, risk control, and information security. Over the past five decades, the publication has evolved from a niche audit-focused newsletter into a broader platform reflecting the challenges of cybersecurity, digital fraud, and compliance management. This paper explores the growth trajectory of EDPACS, analyzing its thematic evolution through bibliometric trends and selected case discussions. The study also considers future directions, particularly the scalability of its insights into emerging areas such as artificial intelligence governance, blockchain-based auditing, cloud security, and quantum era risk management. By situating EDPACS within both historical and contemporary debates in IT governance, the paper argues that the publication is uniquely positioned to remain relevant provided it embraces interdisciplinary perspectives and addresses the increasing convergence of audit, security, and analytics in digital ecosystems. © Copyright 2025 Taylor & Francis–All rights reserved.},
