	abstract = {Indonesia's informal education system continues to face structural challenges such as inadequate infrastructure, limited tutor digital literacy, and low institutional quality. To address these issues, this paper proposes an AI-driven smart framework for Community Learning Centers (PKBM) by integrating the Technology Acceptance Model (TAM) and Self-Determination Theory (SDT). A PRISMA-guided systematic literature review of 292 sources (84 included) and a pilot implementation were conducted to ensure both theoretical rigor and practical validation. The framework adopts a five-layer architecture - Data Intelligence, AI Processing Engine, Smart Content Management, Interaction Interface, and Analytics & Evaluation - while embedding ethical safeguards for data privacy, algorithmic fairness, and system transparency. Empirical results indicate a 34% improvement in learning outcomes, a System Usability Scale (SUS) score of 82.5, an R2 of 0.592 for student engagement, and an adoption rate of 78% among participating PKBM. The novelty of this research lies in the first integrated TAM-SDT model tailored for informal education, supported by a scalable and culturally adaptive AI architecture. Beyond Indonesia, the framework demonstrates transferability potential to other regions with diverse cultural and institutional settings. This study not only contributes to theory by advancing AI adoption models in informal education but also to practice by offering an ethically grounded, sustainable, and replicable framework for community-based learning transformation worldwide. © 2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {AI-driven education; Community Learning Centers; ethical AI; smart education systems; TAM-SDT integration},
