	affiliations = {Clicksoft solutions LLC, NJ, United States},
	abstract = {Agentic AI systems are increasingly deployed in safety-critical domains, demanding both autonomy and assurance. However, conventional agent architectures lack formal mechanisms for runtime verifiability and often rely on opaque black-box policies that are difficult to interpret and debug. In this paper, we propose a novel framework that integrates lightweight quantum verification subroutines into explainable agentic decision loops. These quantum modules serve as real-time safety checkers, ensuring that agent policies satisfy encoded constraints before execution. Coupled with a symbolic trace-based explanation engine, our framework supports provable correctness, semantic reasoning, and auditability of actions. We evaluate our approach across benchmark environments simulating infrastructure control, navigation, and compliance auditing. Our results show significant improvements in failure suppression, explanation fidelity, and verifiability over state-of-the-art baselines. This work represents a step toward building trustworthy AI systems that are not only capable and adaptive but also certifiably correct and transparent at deployment time. © 2025 IEEE.},
