	affiliations = {St.Joseph's Institute of Technology, Department of Information Technology, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {Criminal investigations often involve sifting through large amounts of structured and unstructured data, such as case files, criminal profiles, accomplice connections, and behavioral patterns. Analyzing these records manually takes a lot of time, is prone to mistakes, and can be inefficient, especially in places with limited digital resources. To tackle these issues, we introduce COPS (Criminal Operandi Prediction System), a web application powered by AI. It allows law enforcement personnel to retrieve and analyze criminal data using just one input in natural lan- guage. COPS can extract important details like suspect names, 10- cations, crime descriptions, and partner information. It connects them to existing records through fuzzy matching and semantic analysis. The system shows relevant criminal history, methods of operation, relationships, and predicts likely behaviors based on past data. It is built with modern technologies, including React for the frontend, FastAPI and Python for backend logic, and MongoDB for flexible data storage. Designed to be deployed on- premise, COPS ensures complete data privacy while remaining usable without an internet connection. This paper discusses the architecture, workflow, and implementation of COPS, showing how it can speed up investigations, improve decision-making, and boost public safety through smart crime analysis. © 2025 IEEE.},
