	affiliations = {CA, United States},
	abstract = {Personalized pricing strategies for subscription-based digital products often overlook causal effects and fairness dynamics, instead relying on predictive models that optimize short-term revenue. This creates risks of long-term loyalty erosion, trust decay, and regulatory scrutiny around algorithmic fairness. We propose GTSO++ (Generative Tier Simulation and Optimization++), a simulation-enhanced framework that integrates causal uplift modeling, behavioral fairness auditing, and synthetic persona simulation to optimize tiered pricing strategies while accounting for long-term trust and loyalty dynamics. We train a causal uplift model (X-Learner) on a real-world marketing campaign dataset (Hillstrom E-Mail Analytics) to estimate individual treatment effects on conversion probability. Using these uplift scores, we simulate tier assignments (Basic, Pro, Premium) and evaluate pricing performance under both standard and behaviorally shifted customer populations. Synthetic personas are generated with varying loyalty, price sensitivity, trust, and impulsivity traits to conduct structured sensitivity analyses. We simulate high-impulsivity scenarios, trust decay events, and dynamic loyalty-trust evolution over multiple offer rounds. Generative AI is used to assist in persona realism and provide natural language explanations of observed fairness and loyalty trends, but not for causal model development. Uplift-based tiering outperformed random assignment in improving conversion rates while maintaining initial fairness across loyalty groups. Sensitivity analyses revealed that loyalty and trust degradation significantly impair conversion rates, revenue, and fairness over time, especially under repeated unfair pricing exposures. High impulsivity increased short-term conversions but did not stabilize loyalty trajectories. GTSO++ demonstrates that sustainable subscription pricing requires not only causal targeting but also dynamic modeling of customer loyalty and trust. Our findings highlight the need for fairness-aware, behaviorally resilient pricing optimization frameworks in increasingly regulated and competitive digital markets © 2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Causal Inference; Fairness in Pricing; Generative AI; Multi-Objective Optimization; Subscription Pricing; Uplift Modeling},
