	abstract = {Image classification for pest detection is necessary for precision agriculture related to crop management and has an overall impact on food safety. This project offers an image classification pipeline that uses Spatial Transformer Networks (STN) with a pre-trained ConvNeXt_large backbone. CBAM is incorporated to add spatial and channel attention to enhance the representation and robustness of the model against the transformations of pest images. Training occurs via an AdamW optimizer with a cross-entropy loss function for effective convergence and generalization. Classification reports and Grad-CAM overlays serve as performance metrics that assess the model's predictive capabilities. With a comparative baseline model, the resulting accuracy from the proposed approach is higher - especially in predicting the pest class regardless of orientation or scaling. The results demonstrate that our proposed approach delivers significant advantages over the existing methods. The proposed method achieves an accuracy of 75% and offers a 5% improvement in effectiveness in classifying pests of 102 classes. © 2025 IEEE.},
